<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chandragupta Maurya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded empire 321 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chandragupta Maurya was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a>, which he established in 321 BCE after overthrowing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanda-dynasty">Nanda dynasty</a>, traditionally with the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanakya">Chanakya</a>. He extended his rule across northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucus-i-nicator">Seleucus I</a>, gaining territories in the northwest in exchange for 500 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephants</a>. The treaty established peaceful relations with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chandragupta-maurya.jpg" alt="Chandragupta Maurya" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: आशीष भटनागर at Hindi Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandragupt_maurya_Birla_mandir_6_dec_2009_(31)_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
